  "title": "Ann Widdecombe's Murder Suspect Charged with Preparing Terrorist Acts Against Nigel Farage",
  "summary": "Joshua Kerry, a 28-year-old British man accused of killing the former lawmaker Ann Widdecombe, was charged with planning terror acts, including against Nigel Farage. The Crown Prosecution Service charges him with preparation of terrorist acts, and the investigation involved counter-terrorism police.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Joshua Kerry, 28, of Rotherham in South Yorkshire, was charged by the Crown Prosecution Service on Friday with one count of preparation of terrorist acts.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The charge relates to activity alleged to have taken place between 31 May 2024 and 8 July this year, counter-terrorism police said.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
